# TruScoreGradingSystem --- Module Definitions (v1)

## 1. PURPOSE

Define strict ownership of responsibilities across the codebase.

## 2. MODULE STRUCTURE

/project_root ├── ingestion/ ├── identification/ ├── grading/ ├──
market/ ├── decision/ ├── pipeline/ ├── app/ ├── utils/

## 3. MODULE RESPONSIBILITIES

ingestion: image preprocessing only\
identification: CardSight API calls\
grading: condition analysis (surface, edges, corners, centering)\
market: pricing and population data\
decision: expected value and recommendations\
pipeline: orchestration only\
app: UI and communication\
utils: shared helpers only

## 4. RULES

-   One function = one module\
-   No duplicate logic\
-   No cross-module contamination\
-   No temporary logic outside modules

## 5. REFACTOR STRATEGY

-   Extract working functions\
-   Move to correct module\
-   Replace original with import + call\
-   Do NOT rewrite working logic

## 6. WARNING SIGNS

-   Duplicate functions\
-   Mixed responsibilities\
-   UI calling grading logic\
-   Market logic inside grading

## 7. GOAL

Modules must be isolated, testable, and reusable.
